# S6_tapesearch (D-SESSIONS / D-TAPENEXT, 2026-11-06): a cassette search that finds
# no matching header ahead. The tape is ENCODED at run time (one ASCII file OTHER
# from S6_other.bas, probes/lib/cas_encode.py), not recorded in the session -- an in-session recording
# did not play back repeatably (scratchpad/S6_tape_parked.ses). On the VG-8020 the
# search shows `Skip :OTHER` and then WAITS until Ctrl-STOP (Device I/O error);
# zerobas's TAPION used to give up by itself after ~5 s of silence.
{TAPEASCII OTHER S6_other.bas}
LOAD "CAS:PROG1"
{WAIT 8}
{STOP}
PRINT "A"
{TCL cassetteplayer rewind}
CLOAD "PROG1"
{WAIT 8}
{STOP}
PRINT "B"
{TCL cassetteplayer eject}
CLOAD
{WAIT 8}
{STOP}
PRINT "C"
{TAPEASCII OTHER S6_other.bas}
LOAD "CAS:OTHER"
LIST
